{%- comment -%}
  HIVOLT — snippets/newsletter.liquid
  ───────────────────────────────────
  The footer signup. Rendered by layout/theme.liquid, so it is on every page
  that uses the shared shell.

  Why it exists: /pages/membership already carries a full signup, and almost
  nobody navigates to it. Every other page in the store offered a visitor no
  way to leave an address at all, so a visitor who was not ready to buy left
  and could not be reached again.

  Shopify's native customer form — no app, no third-party script:

      form 'customer'      → creates a customer and sets accepts_marketing
                             true, which is what puts the address in front of
                             Shopify Email
      contact[email]       → the address, validated server-side by Shopify
      contact[tags]        → "newsletter, circuit" — the same pair the
                             membership page applies, so both entry points
                             land in one segment rather than two

  form.posted_successfully? is scoped to the form TYPE, not to this element.
  templates/page.membership.liquid renders its own form 'customer', so on that
  page BOTH would light up after a submit and print the confirmation twice.
  layout/theme.liquid guards the render on the page handle; this file assumes
  that guard rather than repeating it.

  id: 'circuit' makes the form action /contact#circuit, so the redirect after a
  submit lands on the block instead of the top of the page. The confirmation
  takes tabindex="-1" and role="status" so it is announced, not just coloured.
{%- endcomment -%}

<section class="sub" aria-labelledby="sub-h">
  <div class="sub__grid">

    <div class="sub__say">
      <p class="mono sub__eyebrow">The Circuit</p>
      <h2 class="sub__h" id="sub-h">Told first. Nothing else sent.</h2>
      <p class="sub__p">
        One email when a drop is coming, one when it goes live. No weekly
        newsletter, because there isn't one.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="sub__do">
      {%- form 'customer', id: 'circuit' -%}

        {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
          <div class="sub__ok" tabindex="-1" role="status">
            <p class="mono sub__ok-h">You're on the list</p>
            <p class="sub__ok-b">
              Nothing else to do. The next message you get from us will be a
              drop going live — every email carries an unsubscribe link.
            </p>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if form.errors -%}
          <div class="sub__err" tabindex="-1" role="alert">
            <p class="mono sub__err-h">That didn't go through</p>
            <ul class="sub__err-l">
              {%- for field in form.errors -%}
                <li>
                  {%- if field == 'form' -%}
                    {{ form.errors.messages[field] }}
                  {%- else -%}
                    {{ form.errors.translated_fields[field] }} — {{ form.errors.messages[field] }}
                  {%- endif -%}
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="newsletter, circuit">

        <div class="sub__row">
          <div class="sub__f">
            <label class="mono sub__l" for="circuit-email">Email address</label>
            <input class="sub__in" type="email" id="circuit-email"
                   name="contact[email]" autocomplete="email"
                   autocorrect="off" autocapitalize="off" required
                   value="{{ form.email }}"
                   placeholder="you@example.com">
          </div>
          <button class="sub__go" type="submit">Join</button>
        </div>

        <p class="sub__note">
          Unsubscribe from any email. The address is used for drop notices and
          nothing else — it is not sold and it is not passed to an advertiser.
          <a href="/pages/membership">What the list is</a>
        </p>

      {%- endform -%}
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
